@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Read current sprint board
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "SprintBoardPage / BoardView" as page
  participant "IBoardService / BoardService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "BoardsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "GetActiveSprintBoardQueryHandler" as handler
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Open the Board tab of a Scrum project (BoardModeGuard matched SprintBoardPage)
page -> client : activeSprintBoardResource(ActiveSprintBoardQuery: status batch, size, generation);\nsent as GetActiveSprintBoardQuery; the generation stays in the client and stamps the result
client -> access : GET /api/workspaces/{id}/active-sprint/board
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once; sign in with the board as return route
else Authenticated (profile P: every active role reads sprints)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send GetActiveSprintBoardQuery through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-045 batch size 1-100; known status
  alt Invalid batch size or status
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : The board shows the message with Reload board, without Try again or reference ID;\nsprintLoaded emits null
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle GetActiveSprintBoardQuery
    handler -> db : LoadActiveSprintBoardAsync: workspace mode, active sprint, and next planned sprint
    db --> handler : Mode and sprint summary
    alt Workspace not found
      handler --> ctrl : 404
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : BoardView shows Project not found with Back to projects (no Try again or reference ID)\nand emits notFound; on the first one SprintBoardPage calls the layout's refresh()
    else Workspace in Kanban mode (L2-027.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 mode-changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (mode changed)
      client --> page : BoardView emits modeChanged; SprintBoardPage calls ProjectLayoutPage.modeChanged():\nthe header reloads and BoardModeGuard re-matches KanbanBoardPage; sprint plans stay on the Sprints tab
    else No active sprint
      handler --> ctrl : No-active view: the next planned sprint (SprintPeriod), else the latest closed sprint\n(SprintReference, latest closure then ID), or neither; the workspace story total
      ctrl --> client : 200 without board columns
      client --> page : BoardView emits sprintLoaded (sprintId null); the page renders Start for nextPlannedSprint\nand Plan sprint; with none planned, Plan sprint and a router link to latestClosedSprint's history;\nwith no sprints, Plan sprint and Open Work; Add initiative replaces Add story while the story total is 0
    else Active sprint
      handler -> db : L2-024 read current open membership in bounded status batches of at most 100;\nfull column totals and set-based task counts in the same read; no descriptions
      db --> handler : Cards, shared story status, task counts, full column totals
      handler --> ctrl : ActiveSprintBoardResult: sprint ID, name, version, goal, dates, start instant and actor,\ninitial scope and scope-change counts, story, Done and point totals, workspace story total,\nboard and versions
      ctrl --> client : 200 with board and versions
      client --> page : Discard if the board ID or generation is no longer current; otherwise it becomes\nthe latest acknowledged board and BoardView emits sprintLoaded with the header;\nthe page registers Add story, or Add initiative while the workspace story total is 0
      page -> page : SprintBoardPage keeps the header; renders the header card and its actions;\npasses the sprint ID to SprintScopeLogView and the scope and close dialogs;\nan empty sprint keeps all three columns and Add stories
      page --> actor : Columns with Move and the card menu on every card and Remove on unfinished cards
    end
  end
end
group Load more and the reread after a move (kanban move rules)
  actor -> page : Load more in one column, or a move that the server confirmed
  page -> client : Next batch of that column; after a confirmed move, the loaded window\nof the source and destination columns in batches of at most 100
  client --> page : Results with an older generation or another board are discarded; the reread becomes\nthe latest acknowledged board and BoardView emits sprintLoaded with its header, never null in between,\nso the progress totals follow each confirmed move; a failed batch or reread keeps the last header
  note over page
    While a move is pending: other Move controls, card-menu moves, drag and Load more are unavailable;
    "Saving move..." is announced. A rejected move restores the latest acknowledged
    board; an uncertain outcome rereads the affected columns before another move.
    A 500 or 503 ends Failed with the reference ID: an open move or unfinished-tasks dialog
    shows its failed state and no toast appears; with no dialog open, the move-failed toast
    shows the ID and Retry, sent only when chosen. A 404 ends Settled; a removed focused
    card moves focus to the board region.
    A 400 ends Settled: the "Your move wasn't applied" page alert shows the reason with
    Reload board, no Retry and no reference ID (Kanban rule).
    A board-changed 409 shows the page alert on the board (no toast) with Reload board.
    An unexpected 403 restores the acknowledged board and ends Forbidden: any open dialog
    closes and the page shows the "Your access changed" toast without Retry.
    A 409 unfinished-tasks opens UnfinishedTasksDialog instead. A mode-changed 409 restores
    the acknowledged board, ends the move, shows no alert and emits modeChanged.
  end note
end
opt Try again after a failed first batch
  actor -> page : Choose Try again
  page -> page : BoardView emits retryRequested; SprintBoardPage calls ProjectLayoutPage.refresh(), so the header\nand the board reread together
end
opt A committed dialog outcome, an open dialog's unconfirmed, or a layout revision
  page -> page : SprintBoardPage increments its counter; the refresh input of BoardView and SprintScopeLogView\nchanges; the board rereads its first batch with a new generation (sprintLoaded null until it resolves)
end
note over ctrl, db
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043); a failed first-batch read
shows Load failed with Try again (the reference ID only after a 500 or 503; none when the read got
no response); sprintLoaded emits null, so no header actions show.
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
